{
  "dom_id": "step-q86483",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The function $v(t)=8{e}^{t/2}$ gives the volume, in cubic centimeters, of methylated spirit produced by a chemical process $t$ hours after the process begins. Find the instantaneous rate of change of spirit volume as a function of $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "The instantaneous rate of change of the spirit volume is equal to ${v}^{\u2032}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $v(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{e}^{t/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (8{e}^{t/2}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the volume of spirit with respect to time is $4{e}^{t/2}$ cubic centimeters per hour.",
